Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:00:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Data Analytics audit, phase 2-3: export, snapshot, state
 and chart fixes

Root causes found and fixed (see the audit report in docs/):

- Export 500 "reading 'flatMap'": insights / executive_summary blocks with no
  analysisIds were read unguarded by the pptx builder, the compute step, the
  findings report and the viewer. One helper (blockRefs) now answers "which
  analyses does this block read" everywhere; saved reports are normalised on
  PUT. The export route checks there is data before building, builds inside a
  guard, validates the file, and returns a sentence + reference, never the raw
  exception; gaps are reported beside the download.
- Shared snapshot at 0 / n = 0: the builder rewrote a saved analysis's dataset
  with the workspace selector on mount (twice under strict mode); planned
  analyses kept a stale environment; "responses" was the base of whichever
  analysis came back first; publish froze blank reports silently. Publish now
  refuses a blank or partial snapshot unless forced, responses is the largest
  base, and the viewer says "no respondents" instead of drawing zeros.
- Warning wall: per-column base warnings collapse to one sentence, long lists
  fold behind the first three, zero bases show blank not 0.0%, weighted n
  follows the valid base, runner exceptions become a structured error.
- Save / stale: canonical (key-sorted) comparison, one save at a time,
  latest-run-wins, export / save-chart / add-to-report refuse stale results,
  failed save aborts publish, stale errors are cleared, results reload after
  save and a late save can no longer pre-empt a version view.
- Saved charts load a few at a time and show a failure with Try again.
- Question-aware chart selection (questionChart.ts): multi-select, scale,
  numeric, ranking, text, crosstab size and thin bases drive the chart, state
  the denominator and explain why; a saved type the data cannot draw falls
  back and says so.

Tests: analytics 292, studio lib 296, new browser suite
scripts/analytics-audit-test.mjs (16 checks, 7 UI mutations caught); the
unit-level mutations are all caught.

