From: Miures Manager <contact@miures.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:14:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Data Analytics audit, phase 3: one review for every
 analysis before it is kept

The plan generator and the workspace could put analyses in front of the
researcher that could not be computed (a variable not in the survey, a mean of
a text answer, a crosstab with nothing on one axis) or that repeated another
(a chi-square test beside the crosstab that already carries it). They ran,
failed into a warning, and showed as blank / warning-wall results.

- planCheck: validateAnalysis, reviewPlanned, reviewAgainstSaved, signature,
  surveyKnownNames. "Create the planned analyses" now reviews against what the
  researcher already has (planned id or any hand-built analysis that computes
  the same thing) and reports what was blocked or skipped, with the reason.
- The analyses rail separates generated analyses from ones a person built.
- Tests: 8 planCheck unit tests (10/10 mutations caught) + audit-suite section 9.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAcfUsJLu3R4pYxzaj9SU4
